  "id": "COMPOUND:1362 - PROTEIN:1503",
  "verbalization": "Aminophenazone appears to have a mechanistic link to G1/S-specific cyclin-D1 through a series of target interactions. The evidence suggests that Aminophenazone acts as a target of multiple compounds, which in turn target cyclin-D1. Specifically, Aminophenazone is involved in the pathway leading to cyclin-D1, as it is a target of two distinct compounds—6-O-acetyldihydrohelenalin and 5-O-demethylpaxanthonin—both of which are themselves targets of cyclin-D1. This indicates a potential indirect pathway where Aminophenazone may influence cyclin-D1 through these intermediates. The presence of multiple targets and the consistent involvement of cyclin-D1 in the pathway suggest a possible role in cell cycle regulation, particularly in the G1/S transition. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Aminophenazone may modulate cyclin-D1 activity, though further validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and the specific mechanism of action.",
